# jobhunt — candidate profile and filters
# Everything the pipeline knows about you lives here. Edit freely; nothing else hardcodes
# your details. Written 2026-09-19 from the resume text and target list Sahil supplied.

candidate:
  name: Sahil Anower
  short_name: Sahil            # how outreach drafts sign off
  email: sahilanower2@gmail.com
  phone: "+91 6289208895"
  base_city: Hyderabad
  country: India
  links:
    linkedin: https://www.linkedin.com/in/sahil-anower-031030365
    github: https://github.com/SahilAnower
    leetcode: "1000+ problems solved"

# Pasted verbatim-ish into the scoring prompt. Keep it factual and current; this is the
# single biggest lever on score quality.
resume_summary: |
  Backend engineer, ~3 years experience. Currently Software Development Engineer at
  Amazon, Hyderabad (Nov 2025 - present).

  Amazon (Nov 2025 - present), SDE, Hyderabad:
  - Drove international expansion of the "Add-to-Delivery" open-deliveries datapath from
    US into EU5 (DE, FR, IT, ES, UK) and CA. Multi-region, multi-account monitoring across
    5 AWS regions (us-east-1, eu-west-1, eu-central-1, eu-south-2, us-west-2).
  - Authored the technical design for the EU5 Important Info bottom-sheet using Strategy +
    Factory patterns to render ASIN-level legal disclaimers with zero regression risk to a
    shared upstream component. Secured cross-functional and senior-engineer alignment.
  - Re-architected the AtD monitoring AWS CDK package (~500 leaf + 40 composite alarms,
    5 suites, 10 marketplaces) into a 3-layer feature-sliced design, cutting new-marketplace
    onboarding from 11 synchronized edits to 1 with byte-identical alarm/dashboard parity.
  - Engineered AWS CDK self-mutating pipelines shipping composite CloudWatch alarms,
    automated ticketing, and cross-account dashboards across beta and prod.
  - Built a multi-agent GenAI post-incident writing agent (Collator -> Writer -> Validation),
    cutting authoring time from multiple days to same-day.

  Emmes (Mar 2024 - Nov 2024), Associate Software Engineer, Bangalore:
  - Batch file scheduling and parsing with CSVParser for large data workflows.
  - Redis-based distributed rate limiting to protect APIs under load.

  Crudcook (Jun 2023 - Jan 2024), Associate Software Engineer, Chandigarh:
  - Migrated a legacy Node.js monolith to Spring Boot / Java microservices, cutting server
    load and response time ~20%.
  - Integrated Jira, QuickBooks, Stripe and Plaid into an in-house CRM.

  GeeksforGeeks (Feb 2023 - May 2023), MTS Intern (DSA), Noida.

  Projects: EcomEase (Java, Spring Boot, Spring Cloud Gateway, Eureka, OpenFeign,
  RabbitMQ event-driven order processing). ChitChatHub (Node.js, Socket.io, WebRTC, Nginx
  reverse proxy, Redis Pub/Sub, Docker, MongoDB, React).

  Languages: Java, JavaScript, C++. Stack: Spring Boot, Spring Cloud, Node.js, React,
  AWS (CDK, Lambda, AppSync, DynamoDB, CloudWatch), GraphQL, Kafka/RabbitMQ, Redis,
  MySQL/PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Docker, Kubernetes, Jenkins.

  Education: B.Tech Electrical Engineering, Aliah University, Kolkata (Aug 2023), 7.50/10.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- what counts as a match

roles:
  # Lane A is the core, best-supported-by-the-resume target. Lane B is the stretch lane.
  lane_a: Backend / distributed systems / platform engineering (Java, Spring Boot, AWS)
  lane_b: Agentic AI / LLM application engineering

  # Band. Titles carrying more seniority than this are excluded outright below.
  band: IC, SDE I to SDE II (Software Engineer / Software Engineer II / SDE)

filters:
  # A title must match one of these to be considered at all.
  include_titles:
    - software engineer
    - software development engineer
    - software developer
    - sde
    - backend
    - back end
    - back-end
    - full stack
    - fullstack
    - distributed systems
    - platform engineer
    - infrastructure engineer
    - systems engineer
    - cloud engineer
    - developer experience
    - api engineer
    - application engineer
    - java developer
    - member of technical staff
    - ai engineer
    - ml engineer
    - llm
    - genai
    - gen ai
    - agent
    - forward deployed

  # The seniority/scope ceiling, plus non-engineering noise. Checked FIRST — a title
  # matching any of these is dropped however well it matches include_titles.
  # This is the highest-value filter in the file: the feeds are dominated by senior roles.
  # Matched whole-word, and a trailing period is optional — "sr" covers "Sr" and "Sr.", and
  # will not fire inside "SRE".
  exclude_titles:
    - senior
    - sr
    - staff
    - principal
    - lead            # "Lead Engineer" yes; "Leader" needs its own entry, below
    - leader
    - mgr             # NetApp slugs manager as "mgr", so "Mgr Software Engineer" cleared a
                      # list that only had "manager". Same lesson as SMTS/PMTS: every
                      # abbreviation of a band needs its own entry.
    - leadership
    - architect
    - manager
    - director
    - head of
    - vp
    - vice president
    - chief
    - distinguished
    - fellow
    # Salesforce and Adobe write the whole band as an abbreviation, so the spelled-out ceiling
    # never fires. MTS on its own is in band; these four are Senior, Lead, Principal and
    # Distinguished Member of Technical Staff, and they are not.
    - smts
    - lmts
    - pmts
    - dmts
    - intern
    - internship
    - apprentice
    - trainee
    - account executive
    - sales
    - marketing
    - recruiter
    - recruiting
    - payroll
    - accountant
    - counsel
    - designer
    - program manager
    - product manager
    - project manager

  # Phrases blanked out of the title BEFORE exclude_titles runs, for in-band titles that
  # happen to contain a seniority word. The ceiling still applies to the rest of the title,
  # so "Sr Member of Technical Staff" is still dropped.
  exclude_overrides:
    - member of technical staff

  # Lane A subset. Anything matching include_titles but not this is tagged Lane B.
  lane_a_titles:
    - software engineer
    - software development engineer
    - software developer
    - sde
    - backend
    - back end
    - back-end
    - distributed systems
    - platform engineer
    - infrastructure engineer
    - systems engineer
    - cloud engineer
    - java developer

geo:
  # India only. Profile rules out anything needing a visa or relocation abroad.
  country_terms: [india, bharat]
  # No relocation needed — the best outcome.
  home_terms: [hyderabad, telangana, secunderabad]
  # Acceptable, but means relocating. Surfaced with a flag.
  relocation_terms:
    - bangalore
    - bengaluru
    - pune
    - gurgaon
    - gurugram
    - noida
    - delhi
    - ncr
    - chennai
    - mumbai
    - kolkata
    - ahmedabad
    - kochi
    - coimbatore
    - chandigarh
    - jaipur
    - indore
    - nagpur
    - vadodara
    - mysore
    - mysuru
    - trivandrum
    - thiruvananthapuram
  remote_terms: [remote, work from home, wfh, anywhere]

  # true  = a location with no India signal at all is DROPPED.
  # false = it is kept and flagged "location unclear".
  # Keep true for an India-only search: enumerating every foreign city is never complete,
  # and each gap leaks an out-of-country req into the digest. The cost is that reqs whose
  # ATS location field holds a work arrangement ("Hybrid", "In-Office") get dropped unless
  # the platform exposes a real location elsewhere, which fetch.py tries hard to find.
  require_india_signal: true

comp:
  currency: INR
  target_lpa: 45
  floor_lpa: 38              # below this is a discard
  min_fixed_lpa: 28
  # Indian postings almost never publish a band, so this is judged by the scorer from
  # company and level rather than parsed from text. Unknown comp is never a discard.
  note: |
    Current Amazon total is ~45 LPA (19 fixed + bonus/RSU/sign-on), year-1 inflated by a
    non-repeating sign-on and a 5/15/40/40 vest; steady state is nearer 30-34 LPA. So a
    recurring 45 LPA is a real raise, and a 40 LPA offer with 30 LPA fixed may beat the
    current package in cash terms. Flag those rather than discarding.
  dealbreakers:
    - service-based or consultancy comp bands
    - employment bonds or notice-lock clauses
    - equity-heavy offers with a weak fixed base
    - commission or variable-only structures

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- context for scoring

situation: |
  Urgent, clock-driven search. A performance-improvement plan at Amazon is confirmed and
  the plan is to take severance and exit rather than run the process.

  Consequences for scoring:
  - Speed is a real scoring dimension. A 7 that can produce a signed offer in six weeks
    beats a 9 with a four-month loop.
  - The main risk is narrative, not sourcing: a 10-month Amazon tenure, a performance plan,
    and a 12-month gap in 2025. Resume screeners kill that combination; humans who vouch
    for the candidate do not. So weight roles where a referral is plausible.
  - Reason for leaving, the version to use: growth. Team reorganisation and Amazon's shift
    of investment toward AI narrowed the growth path in their org. Never volunteer the
    performance plan; never lie about it if asked directly.
  - Years of experience: ~3. Treat a JD asking for 5+ years as a stretch needing a referral,
    and 8+ as effectively closed without one.

# What the drafter must never put in a message. Lives here, not in draft.py, because draft.py is
# version-controlled and this is the most sensitive thing the pipeline knows.
drafting:
  never_mention:
    - the performance improvement plan
    - the severance or the planned exit
    - the 2025 employment gap
    - the 10-month tenure framed as short
  reason_for_leaving: >-
    growth — a team reorganisation and a shift of investment toward AI narrowed the path.
    Never elaborate beyond this, and never volunteer the performance plan.

